2026-09-11 09:15:00 - Received stdin data: {"session_id":"8c006f4a-e4e6-4318-91fa-e7039b1b1a5f","transcript_path":"/tmp/.claude/projects/-tmp-servicenow-cmdb/8c006f4a-e4e6-4318-91fa-e7039b1b1a5f.jsonl","cwd":"/tmp/servicenow-cmdb","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","agent_id":"aa67dd9b18f9de28b","agent_type":"ue-ca:implementation:template-developer","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/tmp/iss-ue-ca-plugin/claude/uac/ue-ca/skills/retrieving-context/references/template_docs/ue-template-structure.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/iss-ue-ca-plugin/claude/uac/ue-ca/skills/retrieving-context/references/template_docs/ue-template-structure.md","content":"# Universal Extension Template Structure\n\n## Table of Contents\n\n1. [Overview](#overview)\n2. [Template Anatomy](#template-anatomy)\n3. [Identity & Metadata](#1-identity--metadata)\n4. [Execution Configuration](#2-execution-configuration)\n5. [User Interface Fields](#3-user-interface-fields)\n6. [Runtime Components](#4-runtime-components-optional)\n7. [Valid Template](#valid-template)\n8. [Related Documentation](#related-documentation)\n\n---\n\n## Overview\n\nA Universal Extension template is defined in a `template.json` file that describes the extension's identity, execution behavior, user interface fields, and optional runtime components. This document provides a high-level overview of the template structure and its main sections.\n\n## Template Anatomy\n\nEvery `template.json` file consists of four main sections:\n\n```json\n{\n  // 1. IDENTITY & METADATA\n  \"name\": \"My Extension\",\n  \"extension\": \"ue-my-extension\",\n  \"description\": \"What this extension does\",\n\n  // 2. EXECUTION CONFIGURATION\n  \"agentType\": \"Any\",\n  \"exitCodeProcessing\": \"Success Exitcode Range\",\n  \"exitCodes\": \"0\",\n  \"outputReturnType\": \"STDOUT\",\n\n  // 3. USER INTERFACE FIELDS\n  \"fields\": [\n    // Input and output field definitions\n  ],\n\n  // 4. RUNTIME COMPONENTS (Optional)\n  \"commands\": [],\n  \"events\": [],\n  \"environment\": []\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 1. Identity & Metadata\n\nDefines the extension's basic identity and descriptive information such as name, unique identifier, description, and system ID. This section also includes the variable prefix used to generate field-related variables automatically.\n\n**For complete details**, see **ue-template-standard-fields.md**.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Execution Configuration\n\nControls how the extension executes on agents, how success or failure is determined (exit codes, output scanning), and how output is captured and returned. This section includes agent selection, exit code processing, output configuration, execution behavior flags, credentials, script configuration, and logging settings.\n\n**For complete details**, see **ue-template-standard-fields.md**.\n\n---\n\n## 3. User Interface Fields\n\nThe `fields` array defines the extension's user interface - both input fields (user-fillable) and output fields (extension-populated).\n\n### Field Array Structure\n\n```json\n{\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"field_identifier\",\n      \"fieldMapping\": \"Text Field 1\",\n      \"fieldType\": \"Text\",\n      \"label\": \"Display Label\",\n      \"hint\": \"Help text for user\",\n      \"sequence\": 0,\n      \"required\": false,\n      \"fieldValue\": null,\n      // ... field-specific properties\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**For field-specific properties and metadata**, see **ue-template-standard-extension-fields.md**.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Runtime Components (Optional)\n\nOptional components that enable dynamic behavior and external interactions during task execution. This section includes:\n- **Commands**: Runtime operations on task instances (e.g., \"Abort\", \"Pause\")\n- **Events**: External system notifications\n- **Environment Variables**: Predefined environment variables passed to the extension\n\n**For complete details**, see **ue-template-standard-fields.md**.\n\n---\n\n## Valid Template\n\n- [ ] All required top-level properties present\n- [ ] `name` is descriptive and meaningful\n- [ ] `extension` starts with `ue-` and uses hyphens (not underscores)\n- [ ] `templateType` is `\"Extension\"`\n- [ ] `variablePrefix` is lowercase with underscores\n- [ ] `agentType` is valid value\n- [ ] `exitCodeProcessing` and `exitCodes` are compatible\n- [ ] `outputType` and `outputReturnType` are valid\n- [ ] `runtimeDir` is `null`\n- [ ] JSON is valid (no trailing commas, proper quotes)\n- [ ] If any fields defined, all have correct and required properties\n- [ ] If any components defined (commands, events, environment), all have correct and required properties\n\n---\n\n## Related Documentation\n\n- **ue-template-standard-fields.md** - Documentation showing all possible template fields including metadata and runtime components\n- **ue-template-standard-extension-fields.md** - Extension-specific field properties and metadata\n- **ue-template-architect-notes.md** - Best practices, examples, and design patterns\n","numLines":128,"startLine":1,"totalLines":128}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_019o9c8XiWusmPX68732GVQV","duration_ms":5}

