        "text": "All files compile cleanly. The utility implementation is complete.\n\n---\n\nThe output file is `/tmp/servicenow-cmdb/extension-code/src/utility.py`.\n\nIt contains five cohesive modules in a single file (5 utilities, well under 200-line threshold per utility):\n\n**`ServiceNowClient`** \u2014 `requests.Session` wrapper with `HTTPBasicAuth`, JSON headers, and a configurable timeout read from `UE_HTTP_TIMEOUT`. Exposes `get`, `post`, and `put` methods. Maps HTTP 401 \u2192 `AuthenticationError`, 403 \u2192 `AuthorizationError`, 404 \u2192 `ServiceNowValidationError`, 400/422 \u2192 `ServiceNowBusinessRuleError` or `ServiceNowValidationError` (by keyword scan), transport failures \u2192 `ConnectionError`. Credential values are never logged or included in exception messages.\n\n**`parse_ci_class(display_value)`** \u2014 Extracts the raw table name from the `<Label> (<table_name>)` dynamic choice format using a compiled regex. Returns the full string unchanged if no parenthesised suffix is present; returns empty string on empty input.\n\n**`parse_ire_response(response_body)`** \u2014 Parses the identifyreconcile response, validates that `identificationResults` is non-empty, inspects the `errors` list and routes to `CmdbIdentificationError`, `CmdbReconciliationError`, or `ServiceNowValidationError` based on keyword matching. Maps `INSERT/UPDATE/MATCH` \u2192 `CREATED/UPDATED/MATCHED`, derives `SUCCESS` or `PARTIAL_SUCCESS` from the warnings list. Returns an `IREResult` dataclass.\n\n**`print_table`, `print_record_table`, `print_multi_result_note`** \u2014 Thin wrappers around `tabulate` with `tablefmt=\"rounded_outline\"` for all STDOUT output.\n\n**`sanitize_json(data, redact_values, indent)`** \u2014 Recursively replaces matching string values with `\"[REDACTED]\"` before serializing via `json.dumps`. The caller passes `{credential.password}` as the exclusion set."
      }
