        "text": "All tasks are complete. Here is a summary of what was produced.\n\n---\n\n**Files written:**\n\n`/tmp/servicenow-cmdb/extension-code/src/actions/output.py`\nDefines `ActionOutput` with fields covering all five actions (incident, RITM, CI create/update, CI get). `print_output()` is a documented no-op \u2014 STDOUT rendering is done inside each action via utility helpers. `to_dict()` emits only non-None fields into a flat dict for the extension output payload.\n\n`/tmp/servicenow-cmdb/extension-code/src/actions/create_incident.py`\nBuilds the Incident payload from `short_description` (required) plus up to eight optional fields (`caller` \u2192 `caller_id`). Calls `ServiceNowClient.post()`, updates `OutputFields.incident_number` in real-time, prints a `rounded_outline` table via `print_table()`.\n\n`/tmp/servicenow-cmdb/extension-code/src/actions/update_incident.py`\nValidates `incident_sys_id` non-empty; parses `incident_fields_to_update` as JSON (falls back to `{}`). Calls `ServiceNowClient.put()` on `/api/now/table/incident/{sys_id}`.\n\n`/tmp/servicenow-cmdb/extension-code/src/actions/update_ritm.py`\nSame pattern as Update Incident, targeting `/api/now/table/sc_req_item/{sys_id}` and the `ritm_*` output fields.\n\n`/tmp/servicenow-cmdb/extension-code/src/actions/create_update_ci.py`\nCalls `parse_ci_class()` to extract the raw table name, assembles the IRE payload with `name` + any non-empty attributes, optionally adds `source`, calls `ServiceNowClient.post(\"/api/now/identifyreconcile\")`, and delegates response parsing to `parse_ire_response()`.\n\n`/tmp/servicenow-cmdb/extension-code/src/actions/get_ci.py`\nBuilds `sysparm_query` based on `search_by` mode, resolves `sysparm_fields` (defaults to 8 standard fields), calls `ServiceNowClient.get()`. On zero results raises `NotFoundError`. On one or more results: populates the predefined `cmdb_*` output attributes, serializes sanitized JSON via `sanitize_json()`, and calls `print_multi_result_note()` when N > 1.\n\n`/tmp/servicenow-cmdb/extension-code/src/actions/__init__.py`\nImports all five action functions and maps them in `ACTION_MAPPER` using the exact choice values from the template: `\"Create Incident\"`, `\"Update Incident\"`, `\"Update RITM\"`, `\"Create/Update CI\"`, `\"Get CI\"`.\n\nAll 7 files compile cleanly with Python 3.11 and all imported names (`ServiceNowClient`, `parse_ci_class`, `IREResult`, `parse_ire_response`, `print_table`, `print_multi_result_note`, `sanitize_json`, `InputValidationError`, `NotFoundError`, etc.) were verified against their source modules."
